From 15a22cb83d1fb7edbe2fdf2fa5eb5f02dcdc0886 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 09:44:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/22] Tools: game/js/logic/ is the logic that runs without a
 browser (lint, exports, build)

- eslint.config.js: game/js/logic/ and game-data.js get no browser globals (only PB_VERSION and console) and may
  import only each other, util.js, hooks.js and test-globals.js; game-data.js passes as it is.
- tools/to-module.mjs: the logic exports every top-level name, so a unit test can import any of them. game-data.js
  gains `export` on 11 declarations; nothing else changes (an export does nothing when the page runs).
- vite.config.js removes the emptied game/js/logic/ from dist/ like game/js/engine/.
- (tools/check-quick.py's old-name check already reads game/js/logic/: phase 05 made it read game/js recursively.)

No module moves yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LpFSn4GaodAVzjKW5J3oQR
